# Canonical identity for this repository.
#
# The history carries two addresses for the same person: the 22 Aug commits
# were made before the git identity here was set, and everything from 23 Aug
# onward uses the address in `git config user.email`. Left alone, `git
# shortlog -sne` and `git blame` split one author into two, which reads as two
# contributors on a project that has one.
#
# This only affects git's own output — shortlog, log, blame. GitHub does not
# read .mailmap: it attaches a commit to an account by matching the commit
# email against the verified addresses on that account. Both of these are
# already verified on @NailaYaqoob, which is why the contributors graph
# correctly shows a single person with every commit.
#
# Format:  Canonical Name <canonical@email> <other@email>
Naila Yaqoob <nailayaqoob86@gmail.com> <nailaimran8686@gmail.com>
